svfilters.hg19 — licensing of code and of bundled data
======================================================

The License field of DESCRIPTION (Artistic-2.0) applies to the CODE in this
package. Some bundled DATA are derived from third-party sources that carry
their own terms, which Artistic-2.0 neither grants nor overrides.


1. OncoKB content — the `clinically_significant` column of `transcripts`, and
   the OncoKB contribution to its `cancer_gene` column.

   OncoKB (https://www.oncokb.org), a precision oncology knowledge base
   maintained by Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center (MSK), is the source of
   this content. It is redistributed here with the express permission of MSK
   (granted 2026-09-02) and is used under the OncoKB Terms of Use,
   https://www.oncokb.org/terms.

     - Only gene symbols and OncoKB evidence-level labels are included: no
       variant or alteration content, drugs, tumor types, or descriptive text.
       The raw OncoKB downloads are not part of this package.
     - The content is a frozen snapshot: cancer gene list of 2026-01-06,
       biomarker levels (Tx/Dx/Px/R) of 2026-01-12. OncoKB is updated
       continuously. Anyone needing current OncoKB content, or OncoKB data for
       any other purpose, should obtain it directly from https://www.oncokb.org
       under their own registration and terms.
     - The permission covers redistribution of these columns in this package;
       it does not grant further rights to OncoKB content.

   MSK makes no warranties or representations with respect to the OncoKB
   content, and it is not a substitute for professional medical judgment or
   advice.

   Cite: Chakravarty D, et al. OncoKB: A Precision Oncology Knowledge Base.
   JCO Precis Oncol. 2017;2017:PO.17.00011. PMID 28890946. And: Suehnholz SP,
   et al. Quantifying the Expanding Landscape of Clinical Actionability for
   Patients with Cancer. Cancer Discov. 2024;14(1):49-65. PMID 37849038.


2. Literature driver-gene sets — the remainder of the `cancer_gene` column.

   Gene symbols extracted from the supplementary tables of six published
   driver-gene analyses (PMIDs 23539594, 24132290, 24390350, 29056346,
   29625053, 32015527). Copyright in those tables rests with the respective
   publishers; only gene symbols are included here.


3. 2016 literature-based gene list — the `cancer_connection` and `biol_sign`
   columns of `transcripts`, from inst/extdata/cancer_genes_2016-03-05.csv.
   Contains no OncoKB content.
